meta {
  name: Get Application Form Details
  type: http
  seq: 23
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/student/application-forms/my-applications/{{applicationId}}/details?section=personal_details
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  section: personal_details
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{studentAccessToken}}
}

docs {
  Live read of ONE form-step section — for resuming/pre-filling that
  step's page. `section` is required, one of:

  personal_details | family_details | address_details |
  qualification_details | achievements_details | tenth_grade |
  twelfth_grade | undergraduate | pg | diploma | entrance_exam_details |
  declaration

  Each page on the client calls this with its own `section` value rather
  than fetching everything at once.

  Response `data` is just that section's object directly (e.g. for
  `section=personal_details`, `data` is `{ full_name, date_of_birth, ... }`),
  or `{}`/`null` if that step hasn't been filled in yet. Missing/invalid
  `section` -> ValidationError.

  Source differs by section:
  - personal_details / family_details / address_details /
    qualification_details / achievements_details / tenth_grade /
    twelfth_grade / undergraduate / pg / diploma — read live off the
    Student profile (the five academic-record sections are sub-keys
    inside `qualification_details`, also exposed individually here to
    match each screen's own PATCH endpoint one-to-one). NOT the frozen
    per-application snapshot — that's only written once, at Submit
    Application, and isn't exposed by this endpoint. Works regardless of
    the application's form_status.
  - entrance_exam_details / declaration — these are NOT on the Student
    profile, they're stored directly on this specific Application row
    (per-application, not reusable across applications), so they're read
    straight off it instead.
}
